I’ve read McKee–Pinch §5 directly. It is a close precursor: it uses weighted congruences \(\lambda p\equiv\pm\mu q\pmod{k}\), a modulus-squared speedup, and a heuristic search over primes near \(N^{1/4}\). It does not state the claimed \(N^{1/6}\) almost-all theorem. The paper should explain this relationship explicitly.

